// Binding a CALL RESULT that is a reference into a `let` local previously
// had no route (`statement sequence: call: flow call`). The binding now
// routes — a targetless `--check` compiles — and the residual wall is
// downstream: native artifact canonical abstract optimization declines
// `InvalidStructuralTypeIdentity(StructuralTypeId(3))` on the reference
// result's carried type.
//
//   let v: u32   = self.plain();            checks   (scalar result)
//   let v: &u32  = self.borrow_it();        check-green, native-red (this fixture)
//   let v: &[u8] = self.buf.as_slice();     same residual wall (a std method)
//
// A STATEMENT call with a `&mut` argument checks, so it is not calls, and not
// references in argument position -- it is a reference in RESULT position
// reaching a local binding.
//
// SAME GAP as `tests/omega/run/borrows/reference_local_binding_routes`,
// which found that a reference binding routes ONLY for a `&mut` of a
// self-rooted place named directly. A call result is one more producer that
// does not route. The label is not the cause and the phase varies with the
// PRODUCER, which is why this gap looks like several unrelated clusters:
//
//   `&self.size`, `&self.buf[0]`, `&mut self.buf[off]`, a reference recast
//                       -> `statement sequence: local data: structural call binding`
//   a borrow of a plain local, with a transition following
//                       -> `state graph: result custody accounting`
//   `self.buf.as_slice()`
//                       -> `statement sequence: call: flow call`
//   an own machine returning `&u32`   (this fixture)
//                       -> `state graph: operation custody: reference custody`
//   `&self.buf[0]` in a single-body machine with no transition
//                       -> `statement sequence: unsupported statement kind`
//
// Seven labels, one capability. The last row also shows the phase depends on
// the SURROUNDING program, not only the statement: the identical borrow
// reports a different phase once a transition follows it. Do not split this
// into separate items by label, and do not pin a repair on any of the strings.
//
// Progress since: the shared `&` place loans (rows 1-2) now route through
// the shared place-loan arm, and this fixture's own leg cleared the
// result-position stack — leaf-loans gate, `ref` result signature, the
// `EstablishReference` source-effect rejoin, and the verifier's
// reference-shape admission — to its present wall:
//   InvalidReferenceCustody: reference result changes its mapped source type
// (the verifier's call-result source mapping in validation/references.rs).
use omega_language_std::console;
use omega::language::core::binding;

data Main {
    console: Binding<Console>;
    count: u32;
}

machine Main::borrow_count(main: &Main) -> &u32 {
    transition { _ -> out(main) }
    state out(main: &Main) -> &u32 { &main.count }
}

machine Main::main(main: &mut Main) reaches Console {
    main.count = 3;
    let borrowed: &u32 = Main::borrow_count(main);
    main.console.exit_process(0);
}
